{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Concept of Intellectual Property Infringement "}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about intellectual property infringement. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.  Define strategies to make terms of reference and supplier assessment processes, in technology acquisition, based on established protocols. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negotiation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Passive of Modal Verbs: May"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>We use<strong> may </strong>in<strong> passive voice </strong>when we want to express factual possibility.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Intellectual property infringement, or IP, may be defined as an act of breaking the law. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Businesses may be involved in different risks."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Some risks may be leading to limitless fines or custodial sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong>May</strong> in <strong>passive voice</strong> refers to an action that can be probably done by an unknown or non-relevant agent.</p>  <p>Examples:</p> <ul> <li><i>Intellectual property <strong>may be copied</strong></i></li> <li><i>Piracy <strong>may be punished</strong> in our country.</i></li> </ul>  <p>The grammatical structure you need to use <strong>may</strong> in the <strong>passive voice</strong>:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject + <strong>may </strong>+ <strong>be</strong> + <strong>verb in past participle</strong> + complement.</p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Negative Questions with Can to Ask for Agreement "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p><strong>Negative </strong>tag <strong>questions</strong> with <strong>can</strong> are used to request the <strong>agreement </strong>of a second speaker when something is possible to happen.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It can include technology, can't it?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Viruses and malware can also be a risk, they?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Infringement can cause reputational risks, can't it?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>We can use <strong>negative questions </strong>with <strong>can</strong> to ask for confirmation of an idea or to reinforce the idea of something you know is totally true.</p> <p>To create a&nbsp;<strong>negative question</strong> with<strong> can</strong> when asking for <strong>agreement</strong>, first, you need to make an affirmative sentence to express the idea you want to be agreed with.</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>You <strong>can</strong> get a fine when distributing products with no permission.&nbsp; </i></p> <p>Afterwards, you introduce the negative question to ask for the agreement. It has to be composed by <strong>can&rsquo;t</strong> plus the <strong>subject pronoun</strong> used in the affirmative sentence.</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>You <strong>can</strong> get a fine when distributing products with no permission.&nbsp; <strong>Can&rsquo;t </strong>you?</i></p> <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "infringement "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a violation or act that breaks a law "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Infringement can cause reputational risks, can't it?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "law "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an agreement stipulated by a legislature"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Intellectual property infringement, or IP, may be defined as an act of breaking the law."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "own "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have something of your possession "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Intellectual property rights may be infringed when a product is used without an authorization or permission from the person who owns this product."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "piracy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the unauthorized use of copyrighted material  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  What we usually call piracy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "counterfeit "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a copy or imitation of something without the owner\u00b4s permission "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Everything that includes infringement to copyrights and trade mark, or even selling counterfeits."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fine "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a quantity of money that is supposed to be paid because of doing something against the law "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some risks may be leading to limitless fines or custodial sentences."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a well-known company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find information about the criminal IP offenses that can affect its productivity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose the most important offenses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Organize the information in a poster."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain to your partners the most important offenses that affect the company. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find information about the criminal IP offenses that affect a company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I choose the most important data. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a poste with the most important information. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain to my partners the most important offenses that affect the company chosen. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n7le02ob09re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n7le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>Peter: </strong>Hey! Do you remember we were going to talk about the intellectual property of infringement yesterday?</p>\n<p><strong>Wendy:&nbsp; </strong>Can&rsquo;t we discuss it today?</p>\n<p><strong>Peter:&nbsp; </strong>Sure.&nbsp; Intellectual property infringement, or IP, may be defined as an act of breaking the law when distributing and selling products without permission.</p>\n<p><strong>Wendy: </strong>Intellectual property rights may be infringed when a product is used without an authorization or permission from the person who owns this product. Right?</p>"}, {"time": "28500", "image": "enpe8n7le02ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p><strong>Peter: </strong>Yes!&nbsp; What we usually call piracy.</p>\n<p><strong>Wendy: </strong>It can include technology. Can&rsquo;t it?</p>\n<p><strong>Peter: </strong>Exactly. Everything that includes infringement to copyrights and trade mark, or even selling counterfeits.</p>\n<p><strong>Wendy</strong>: What about the risks connected to this infringement?</p>\n<p><strong>Peter</strong>: Businesses may be involved in different risks if IP crime is evident within the work environment. Some risks may be leaded to limitless fines or custodial sentences.</p>\n<p><strong>Wendy: </strong>Viruses and malware can also be a risk. Can&rsquo;t they?</p>\n<p><strong>Peter: </strong>Absolutely! There are some activities that may be related to something done directly by the organization.</p>\n<p><strong>Wendy</strong>: Infringement can cause reputational risks, can't it?</p>"}, {"time": "75000", "image": "enpe8n7le02ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p><strong>Peter:&nbsp; </strong>Of course! That&rsquo;s even worse. The reputation of a business represents respect and trust from partners and customers. Any criminal action may be reflected on how other businesses deal with you.</p>\n<p><strong>Wendy: </strong>What are some criminal IP offences in a company?</p>\n<p><strong>Peter: </strong>For instance, employees selling copies of works; using the company&rsquo;s equipment to make infringing actions throughout the internet or to let visitors sell pirated items.</p>\n<p><strong>Wendy: </strong>Or using unlicensed software. Infringement may be committed even if the agent doesn&rsquo;t mean to do it.</p>\n<p><strong>Peter: </strong>Besides, this type of crime may be evidenced on the productivity of the company.</p>\n<p><strong>Wendy: </strong>That&acute;d be such a shame to affect your work in such a silly way.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n7le02ob09re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about the concept of intellectual property infringement. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " In which situation have you copied or used work from others?"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss the risks connected to intellectual property rights infringement."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about some criminal IP offenses in a company."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How is piracy punished in your country?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Talking About Piracy! "}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "img_path": ""}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Disc